  "title": "MediaAssetSource",
  "description": "What a media resource is built from. A URL is streamed by the browser, which owns the transfer for the whole life of the element and never holds more than it is playing. A blob is data the application already owns - an acquired source, a container entry, a cached representation - and the element reads it through an object URL the resource keeps alive for as long as it exists.",
